BASELINE (raw log, no structured inference)
  They're planning a 4-night Lisbon trip with Sam — Thu to Mon in the first week of October (Sam can't do the second week) — with a self-imposed budget of £900 all in for two people, flights and rooms, and an explicit note to themselves: get the numbers in one place, don't book anything. Across three separate sittings (Tue, Thu, Sun) they kept revisiting the same three pages rather than making progress: Skyward flights London Gatwick–Lisbon (Thu 2 Oct 07:15 from £84 one way, Mon 6 Oct 19:40 from £96 one way, hold baggage excluded), Casa Alfama (double city view €148, river view €176, breakfast included, €2 per person per night tourist tax at the hotel), and Miradouro Rooms (standard double €119, breakfast €14 per person, free cancellation until seven days before check-in). On Thursday they pasted three links into a document — that's the only artefact so far. Sunday they searched "lisbon early october weather" and then spent eleven minutes on the Casa Alfama rates table before leaving the desk again. So the dates line up neatly with the flights on offer, but no totals have been worked out and no choice has been made between the two hotels.
