    → Convert at a stated rate so the £900 line is testable — at roughly €1.15/£, Casa Alfama city view lands near £889 all in and Miradouro with breakfast near £871. Both are within £900 only if hold baggage is £0, so make that assumption visible rather than buried.
    → Resolve the two unknowns that could break the budget: what Skyward charges for hold baggage, and whether Miradouro also levies the €2 per person per night tourist tax (their page doesn't mention it, Casa Alfama's does).
    → Note the one genuine differentiator between the hotels: Miradouro offers free cancellation until seven days before check-in, and Casa Alfama's page says nothing about cancellation. Worth checking before treating the two as interchangeable on price.
    → Actually answer the weather question they searched on Sunday and abandoned — one line in the document on early-October Lisbon temperatures and rain, enough to settle whether river view is worth the extra €112.
    → Keep to their own instruction: assemble the numbers only, don't book. Flag that the £84/£96 fares are "from" prices and may drift, so if they stall for another week the totals will need redoing.
